WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:18.146
So if this were back in

00:00:18.348 --> 00:00:19.178
2011,

00:00:19.392 --> 00:00:20.883
this is what we would call

00:00:21.365 --> 00:00:22.195
an S update.

00:00:22.277 --> 00:00:25.380
The iPhone 18 Pro is basically an
iPhone 17 Pro with a chip update,

00:00:25.582 --> 00:00:27.588
a camera upgrade, and better battery life,

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:30.820
plus some new colors to make sure
people know it's the new one...

00:00:30.902 --> 00:00:32.959
That's an S update if we've ever seen one.

00:00:33.041 --> 00:00:35.226
And I think it's tempting
to be disappointed in that,

00:00:35.308 --> 00:00:38.264
but after using it for the past week,
I actually think it's underrated.

00:00:38.346 --> 00:00:40.800
I know, I know.
Cue all the shill comments.

00:00:40.882 --> 00:00:43.544
"What do you mean a $1,200
iPhone is underrated??"

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:46.322
I said underrated, not underpriced.

00:00:46.524 --> 00:00:47.510
It's expensive,

00:00:48.232 --> 00:00:49.576
but it's underrated.

00:00:49.658 --> 00:00:50.825
For two straight years now,

00:00:50.907 --> 00:00:54.248
the Pro iPhone has gone under the radar
and sort of lived in the shadow of

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:55.914
Apple trying their riskier new ideas

00:00:56.426 --> 00:00:57.256
on other phones.

00:00:57.338 --> 00:00:59.212
Last year,
the iPhone Air stole the spotlight.

00:00:59.294 --> 00:01:01.895
That's about the only thing
anyone wanted to talk about...

00:01:01.977 --> 00:01:04.254
This year,
it's all about the first folding iPhone.

00:01:04.336 --> 00:01:05.166
The Duo.

00:01:05.248 --> 00:01:07.657
The flagship Pro iPhone has not
had a groundbreaking new

00:01:07.739 --> 00:01:09.228
feature in over a decade now,

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:11.556
like,
that's what the other models are for.

00:01:12.118 --> 00:01:13.985
But in the Pro iPhone, you will find

00:01:14.187 --> 00:01:15.017
simply

00:01:15.231 --> 00:01:16.617
the best...
iPhone that they make.

00:01:16.699 --> 00:01:18.187
And it's been quietly getting

00:01:18.669 --> 00:01:21.187
really good.
So let's start with the camera system.

00:01:21.269 --> 00:01:22.099
Right?

00:01:22.313 --> 00:01:24.027
Really, there isn't much physically new.

00:01:24.109 --> 00:01:27.208
We're looking at the same three
cameras as last year's 17 Pro.

00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:29.978
A 48-megapixel primary camera,
48-megapixel ultrawide,

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:31.517
and 48-megapixel 4x telephoto.

00:01:31.599 --> 00:01:34.580
But the main camera now gets
this variable aperture lens...

00:01:34.662 --> 00:01:38.526
So for the entire history of the iPhone
and basically every other smartphone

00:01:38.608 --> 00:01:39.928
that's not made by Samsung,

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:40.966
smartphones have had

00:01:41.168 --> 00:01:42.767
fixed aperture lenses.
You know,

00:01:42.849 --> 00:01:45.822
you'd see that aperture as
one of the camera stats.

00:01:45.904 --> 00:01:48.643
It would be like f/2.2 or f/2.0...
or f/1.8.

00:01:48.725 --> 00:01:51.005
Fellow camera nerds already
know all about this,

00:01:51.087 --> 00:01:52.826
but essentially the lower the number,

00:01:52.908 --> 00:01:56.370
the bigger the relative aperture and
the more light that lens is letting

00:01:56.452 --> 00:01:57.710
through to hit that sensor.

00:01:57.792 --> 00:01:58.873
And that's what we all want.

00:01:58.955 --> 00:02:01.820
The biggest aperture possible for
the most light hitting the sensor...

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:03.816
most of the time.

00:02:03.898 --> 00:02:07.152
But my fellow photography nerds
also already know that sometimes

00:02:07.234 --> 00:02:08.820
you want a little more in focus.

00:02:09.022 --> 00:02:12.223
So you can always open up the
aperture and have it wide open to

00:02:12.305 --> 00:02:14.725
let more light in to hit the sensor.
But also now

00:02:15.317 --> 00:02:16.147
the background

00:02:16.361 --> 00:02:17.191
is blurrier.

00:02:17.273 --> 00:02:19.906
But if you want more in focus
and you want it to be more sharp,

00:02:19.988 --> 00:02:22.446
you can stop down that lens
to something like this.

00:02:22.928 --> 00:02:25.436
Which of course is letting less light in,
but is now

00:02:25.998 --> 00:02:28.854
more in focus, a sharper overall image...
And then of course

00:02:29.496 --> 00:02:30.609
there's a middle ground.

00:02:30.691 --> 00:02:34.691
So the iPhone 18 Pro gets a variable
aperture that opens all the way

00:02:34.773 --> 00:02:36.492
up to a new maximum of f/1.48,

00:02:36.574 --> 00:02:37.512
which is awesome.

00:02:37.594 --> 00:02:40.214
But it can also stop
down in stages to f/1.8,

00:02:40.296 --> 00:02:42.435
fold...
f/2.8 or f/4 when you want to,

00:02:42.517 --> 00:02:46.457
and apparently third-party apps
will be able to do infinite stages,

00:02:46.538 --> 00:02:48.858
so smoothly moving through this range...

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:51.739
Anyway,
how much of a difference does this make?

00:02:51.821 --> 00:02:52.651
Well,

00:02:52.733 --> 00:02:55.248
from a whole bunch of photos
I've taken in a whole bunch

00:02:55.330 --> 00:02:57.549
of different situations...
on this phone,

00:02:57.631 --> 00:03:00.426
it actually doesn't really
make a huge difference.

00:03:00.508 --> 00:03:01.519
It's pretty subtle.

00:03:01.601 --> 00:03:03.187
Like this is wide open f/1.48

00:03:03.389 --> 00:03:04.227
and this is f/4.

00:03:04.309 --> 00:03:07.621
And you can see more is in
focus here with that background.

00:03:07.703 --> 00:03:08.533
Again, f/1.48,

00:03:08.747 --> 00:03:09.577
f/4,

00:03:09.791 --> 00:03:11.083
more sharpness, deeper plane of focus.

00:03:11.165 --> 00:03:14.420
It's one of the more subtle things
that you can change about a photo.

00:03:15.142 --> 00:03:15.972
So, you know,

00:03:16.054 --> 00:03:18.446
can the regular person tell
the difference between f/1.48

00:03:18.528 --> 00:03:19.607
and f/4 at first glance?

00:03:20.249 --> 00:03:21.891
Not really.
But also,

00:03:21.973 --> 00:03:24.958
can the regular person
tell the difference between

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:27.654
4800 Kelvin and 5400 Kelvin white balance?

00:03:28.136 --> 00:03:29.035
Also not really.

00:03:29.117 --> 00:03:32.045
And the difference between a 60th
of a second and a 48th of a second

00:03:32.127 --> 00:03:33.639
shutter speed is also pretty subtle.

00:03:33.721 --> 00:03:35.964
But that's what these
Pro tools are all about,

00:03:36.046 --> 00:03:36.876
in my opinion.

00:03:36.958 --> 00:03:40.512
Helping creative people make what they're
trying to make slightly easier and

00:03:40.594 --> 00:03:43.797
giving them more control over more
parts of the image to do that.

00:03:44.279 --> 00:03:47.835
So adding that variable aperture is
just one more thing you can control,

00:03:47.917 --> 00:03:50.918
whether it's to bring the
background slightly more into focus

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:53.339
or have slightly sharper overall images,

00:03:53.421 --> 00:03:56.776
or even to mess with the little
point lights making artistic-looking

00:03:56.858 --> 00:03:58.595
starburst shapes when you stop down,

00:03:58.677 --> 00:04:01.677
thanks to the six aperture blades
not being a perfect circle,

00:04:01.759 --> 00:04:02.941
little stuff like that...

00:04:03.023 --> 00:04:03.952
For those wondering,

00:04:04.034 --> 00:04:06.276
auto mode seems to mostly
default to f/1.48...

00:04:06.358 --> 00:04:08.095
or f/1.8.
The brighter two apertures,

00:04:08.297 --> 00:04:10.287
just to let as much light in as possible.

00:04:10.369 --> 00:04:11.565
pretty much all the time.

00:04:11.647 --> 00:04:14.630
And I never saw it actually
automatically close beyond that,

00:04:15.112 --> 00:04:16.971
but that doesn't actually surprise me.

00:04:17.053 --> 00:04:20.088
And the new f/1.48 max aperture
kind of flew under the radar.

00:04:20.170 --> 00:04:21.110
That is really nice.

00:04:21.192 --> 00:04:25.146
And it means shutter speeds can be faster,
you can freeze action a little more,

00:04:25.228 --> 00:04:28.160
and ISOs can be lower for
slightly less noise in low light.

00:04:28.242 --> 00:04:29.515
So why is it underrated?..

00:04:29.597 --> 00:04:30.610
Well, as you can see,

00:04:30.692 --> 00:04:34.729
it's not making a huge difference on this
camera with this generation of phone.

00:04:34.811 --> 00:04:35.641
But...

00:04:35.723 --> 00:04:37.544
but variable apertures
make a bigger difference,

00:04:37.746 --> 00:04:41.209
the bigger the sensor is,
as you can see with this huge sensor here.

00:04:41.291 --> 00:04:43.268
And if you've been subscribed for a bit,

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:46.562
you also know I've reviewed some
other phones in the past couple

00:04:46.644 --> 00:04:48.363
years with these absolutely huge...

00:04:48.445 --> 00:04:49.393
1-inch-type sensors.

00:04:49.475 --> 00:04:51.606
Just absolutely massive, right?
And on those

00:04:51.808 --> 00:04:55.329
the natural depth of field from the
photos they take is super shallow.

00:04:55.411 --> 00:04:56.241
But

00:04:56.455 --> 00:04:57.843
we've also noticed it's
sometimes too shallow.

00:04:57.925 --> 00:05:00.482
Like I'll take a photo of a
close-up subject and it...

00:05:00.564 --> 00:05:03.951
it'll look kind of bad because the
object isn't even entirely in focus,

00:05:04.033 --> 00:05:07.176
and sometimes autofocus is a bit
slower because the plane of focus

00:05:07.258 --> 00:05:10.157
is so shallow it'll miss and
it'll have to hunt a little bit.

00:05:10.239 --> 00:05:12.942
And so that variable aperture
feature would be awesome...

00:05:13.024 --> 00:05:13.854
on those sensors.

00:05:13.936 --> 00:05:17.231
So if this feature sticks around
long enough until the iPhone gets

00:05:17.313 --> 00:05:18.750
to those much bigger sensors,

00:05:18.952 --> 00:05:20.651
that's when it becomes a huge win.

00:05:21.213 --> 00:05:25.165
So ideally on the way there we can see
it start to get more and more refined.

00:05:25.247 --> 00:05:27.104
And maybe some other camera phones...

00:05:27.186 --> 00:05:28.047
bring it back too.

00:05:28.609 --> 00:05:29.889
Shoutout to the Galaxy S9.

00:05:29.971 --> 00:05:33.638
Apple taking a page out of Google's book
and adding more granular Pro controls to

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:35.351
the camera app of just the Pro phones

00:05:35.833 --> 00:05:38.806
honestly makes a bigger difference
to the user experience than any

00:05:38.888 --> 00:05:40.194
of the hardware in my opinion.

00:05:40.276 --> 00:05:43.249
They've always had the same simple
camera app across every iPhone,

00:05:43.331 --> 00:05:45.980
which I think kind of hamstrung
the Pro phones for a while.

00:05:46.062 --> 00:05:49.359
So you'd always count on grabbing like
the best third-party camera app to

00:05:49.441 --> 00:05:51.251
actually get the most out of the camera.

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:53.775
But now this stock camera app is great.

00:05:54.277 --> 00:05:55.902
You can hold down this bar...

00:05:55.984 --> 00:05:59.493
and add whatever you want up
here in whatever order you want.

00:05:59.695 --> 00:06:00.555
Shutter speed...

00:06:00.637 --> 00:06:02.263
format, there's manual focus,

00:06:02.465 --> 00:06:04.325
and oh my God, there's finally...

00:06:04.407 --> 00:06:05.562
manual white balance.

00:06:05.644 --> 00:06:07.421
Now that is so sick.
So hey Apple,

00:06:07.503 --> 00:06:10.954
as long as you're still in the mood
for making these Pro phones more pro,

00:06:11.036 --> 00:06:12.552
I have a couple more suggestions.

00:06:13.274 --> 00:06:15.757
One, can you let us,
while we're recording log video,

00:06:15.839 --> 00:06:16.669
can we get a Rec.

00:06:16.751 --> 00:06:19.919
709 preview of what it will look
like so we can get exposure right...

00:06:20.001 --> 00:06:22.629
instead of looking like the
flat log as we're recording?

00:06:22.711 --> 00:06:24.708
That would be nice.
Also,

00:06:24.910 --> 00:06:26.912
can you finally let us record

00:06:27.474 --> 00:06:28.304
8K...
video

00:06:28.992 --> 00:06:29.822
please?

00:06:29.904 --> 00:06:32.575
The sensor's big enough,
it's 48 megapixels,

00:06:32.777 --> 00:06:33.607
just 8K 30.

00:06:33.689 --> 00:06:37.804
You even just added in iOS 27 this new
setting where we can set a limit to

00:06:37.886 --> 00:06:41.657
how much storage we want our ProRes
footage to take up so it never

00:06:41.739 --> 00:06:43.116
goes over that maximum...

00:06:43.198 --> 00:06:45.684
I swear, Apple,
this is now the perfect time

00:06:46.236 --> 00:06:47.906
to add that 8K.
It'll be great.

00:06:47.988 --> 00:06:50.672
Now.
Okay, we got to talk about this new chip.

00:06:50.754 --> 00:06:53.205
The 18 Pro and 18 Pro Max have the new...

00:06:53.287 --> 00:06:54.935
A20 Pro chip inside.
Side note,

00:06:55.017 --> 00:06:58.104
are they going to sync up the
chip name and the phone name ever?

00:06:58.186 --> 00:06:59.886
Because 18 and 20, and the 19, 21...

00:06:59.968 --> 00:07:02.006
Am I the only one bothered by that?
Maybe.

00:07:02.006 --> 00:07:02.836
Anyway,

00:07:03.050 --> 00:07:03.880
this is

00:07:04.094 --> 00:07:04.924
a new...

00:07:05.006 --> 00:07:07.918
2-nanometer chip inside alongside
the simultaneously announced M6.

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:11.580
And after using this
phone for the past week,

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:15.529
I really do think this
chip is highly underrated.

00:07:15.611 --> 00:07:16.441
Now,

00:07:16.523 --> 00:07:18.050
I could try to show this
with benchmark scores,

00:07:18.132 --> 00:07:20.373
you know,
that shows peak improvement in power,

00:07:20.455 --> 00:07:22.547
of course,
but that's not the whole story...

00:07:22.629 --> 00:07:24.772
I could also try to show this with,
you know,

00:07:24.854 --> 00:07:27.836
whipping around iOS and multitasking
and how fast things open,

00:07:28.038 --> 00:07:28.994
but honestly, it's...

00:07:29.076 --> 00:07:32.089
it's fast on every new iPhone,
that isn't impressive anymore.

00:07:32.171 --> 00:07:34.975
I think the best way to show this...
is by seeing

00:07:35.177 --> 00:07:36.298
all of that...
and...

00:07:36.380 --> 00:07:39.304
getting a battery life
that's meaningfully longer.

00:07:39.386 --> 00:07:41.049
And...
in the same size phone.

00:07:41.131 --> 00:07:44.024
typically with an S update or you know,
the chip update, we see like,

00:07:44.106 --> 00:07:45.446
here's the bump in performance...

00:07:45.528 --> 00:07:46.912
You know, it's just more powerful.

00:07:46.994 --> 00:07:49.542
It's not gonna be more efficient
or have better battery life,

00:07:49.624 --> 00:07:50.790
but okay, more power,
great.

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:53.876
Or...
you'll see like, here's more efficiency.

00:07:53.958 --> 00:07:58.170
It's not gonna be more powerful,
but at least the battery life is longer.

00:07:58.372 --> 00:07:59.761
Cool...
But to see both...

00:07:59.843 --> 00:08:02.390
in one chip update get
significantly better,

00:08:03.350 --> 00:08:05.210
that's the 2-nanometer effect right there.

00:08:05.292 --> 00:08:08.240
Now, behind the scenes,
they've talked a little bit about this,

00:08:08.322 --> 00:08:11.078
but they moved the DRAM off of
the CPU where it was stacked

00:08:11.160 --> 00:08:12.184
before and put it next.

00:08:12.726 --> 00:08:14.087
So it's still really close by.

00:08:14.169 --> 00:08:15.722
But that lets them put this new...

00:08:15.804 --> 00:08:18.127
3x surface area vapor
chamber directly on the CPU,

00:08:18.209 --> 00:08:19.899
which lets them cool it much better.

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:23.928
So is the power in the chip reaching
literally M1 and M2 level is going

00:08:24.010 --> 00:08:25.702
to matter for most everyday people?

00:08:26.264 --> 00:08:28.361
Absolutely not.
But hey, at the highest end,

00:08:28.443 --> 00:08:31.453
there are some people doing
heavy gaming for long sessions...

00:08:31.535 --> 00:08:35.103
or even like me shooting a ton of 4K
video outside when it's really hot.

00:08:35.185 --> 00:08:39.056
I can't tell you how hot the iPhone has
gotten while shooting autofocus videos

00:08:39.138 --> 00:08:40.770
in the summer here in New Jersey.

00:08:41.110 --> 00:08:43.976
But having this huge new vapor
chamber and connected mid

00:08:44.058 --> 00:08:45.377
frame for better cooling...

00:08:45.459 --> 00:08:46.778
definitely helps with that.

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:48.180
That's what the Pro is for.

00:08:48.262 --> 00:08:51.242
And then obviously bursty stuff
is still going to be great.

00:08:51.324 --> 00:08:52.747
It's a modern iPhone.
But now,

00:08:52.829 --> 00:08:55.135
like exporting videos
is significantly faster,

00:08:55.777 --> 00:08:57.096
image processing is faster,

00:08:57.178 --> 00:08:58.358
and actually the AI stuff.

00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:00.468
So now that the neural engine is doubled,

00:09:00.670 --> 00:09:03.306
it is actually running this like,
I know it's just Siri,

00:09:03.388 --> 00:09:06.363
and I honestly didn't think it
would matter that much for this,

00:09:06.445 --> 00:09:07.275
but

00:09:07.970 --> 00:09:11.563
Siri has been running pretty slow on some,
even some newer phones,

00:09:11.645 --> 00:09:13.600
like even the iPhone 16, which was...

00:09:13.682 --> 00:09:15.472
built from the ground up for AI...

00:09:15.554 --> 00:09:18.336
But even on those phones,
it's running kind of slow,

00:09:18.418 --> 00:09:22.190
but it is running a lot of that stuff
where Siri has to work on-device

00:09:22.752 --> 00:09:25.424
much faster...
So that's another thing that's nice.

00:09:25.506 --> 00:09:26.609
Honestly, this chip

00:09:27.091 --> 00:09:30.252
gets me excited for the
next-generation MacBook Neo.

00:09:30.894 --> 00:09:32.184
That's how good it is.

00:09:32.266 --> 00:09:33.806
Because the MacBook Neo...

00:09:33.888 --> 00:09:34.866
runs the A18 Pro.

00:09:34.948 --> 00:09:37.718
The binned A18 Pro with 8 gigs of RAM.
This...

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:39.579
A20 Pro with 12 gigs of RAM

00:09:40.141 --> 00:09:42.126
would kill in the MacBook Neo.

00:09:42.208 --> 00:09:44.952
It's essentially an M1-level chip.
So I...

00:09:45.594 --> 00:09:46.979
I'm excited for that.

00:09:47.061 --> 00:09:49.271
If you haven't already
watched my whole video,

00:09:49.353 --> 00:09:50.566
on the ridiculous scale...

00:09:50.648 --> 00:09:54.104
of these processors where I shrink
down and walk around on these chips,

00:09:54.186 --> 00:09:55.947
I'll link that below the like button.

00:09:56.029 --> 00:09:58.040
It took a lot to work on that and make it.

00:09:58.122 --> 00:10:00.382
It's one of my favorite
things we've ever done.

00:10:01.044 --> 00:10:01.874
But...

00:10:01.956 --> 00:10:04.540
that was based on the last
generation's 3-nanometer architecture.

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:08.446
This is a new 2-nanometer node
that just proves Moore's law

00:10:08.648 --> 00:10:09.734
still isn't dead...

00:10:09.816 --> 00:10:12.808
And we're closing in on
transistors the size of...

00:10:12.890 --> 00:10:13.976
individual...
atoms.

00:10:14.618 --> 00:10:15.642
It's pretty crazy.

00:10:16.284 --> 00:10:17.114
So, okay,

00:10:17.196 --> 00:10:21.304
the last big bullet point for this new
iPhone was them touting the longest

00:10:21.386 --> 00:10:23.579
battery life ever in iPhones,
which...

00:10:23.579 --> 00:10:24.409
Okay, yeah,

00:10:24.491 --> 00:10:27.097
I would hope that you're improving
your battery life on your

00:10:27.179 --> 00:10:28.583
highest-end phones every year.

00:10:29.295 --> 00:10:30.749
But if you remember...
last year

00:10:31.391 --> 00:10:34.034
they finally did the thing
that we were all hoping for,

00:10:34.116 --> 00:10:36.363
the iPhone Air really
freed up the iPhone 17...

00:10:36.445 --> 00:10:37.275
Pro...

00:10:37.357 --> 00:10:38.889
to be the most pro
version of the iPhone yet.

00:10:38.971 --> 00:10:42.259
And they just went ahead and made it
thicker and heavier and gave it

00:10:42.341 --> 00:10:45.132
the biggest batteries the
iPhone's ever had and was pretty

00:10:45.214 --> 00:10:46.569
universally praised for that.

00:10:46.651 --> 00:10:47.843
So the fact that these 18

00:10:48.045 --> 00:10:49.440
Pros make another significant

00:10:49.642 --> 00:10:51.547
leap is actually kind of interesting...

00:10:51.629 --> 00:10:53.839
On stage,
they were saying all these numbers,

00:10:53.921 --> 00:10:57.304
you know, 36 hours of video playback,
30 hours of mixed usage, blah,

00:10:57.386 --> 00:10:59.818
blah, blah...
That's never meant very much to me.

00:10:59.900 --> 00:11:03.270
But the stat that did stick
to me was that the 18...

00:11:03.352 --> 00:11:04.182
Pro

00:11:04.396 --> 00:11:07.402
has the same battery life expectation...
as the 17...

00:11:07.402 --> 00:11:08.557
Pro...
Max.

00:11:09.430 --> 00:11:10.496
And it does!

00:11:10.578 --> 00:11:13.304
I have been mostly testing
the smaller 18 Pro all week,

00:11:13.386 --> 00:11:14.216
and...

00:11:14.298 --> 00:11:17.440
turns out this is easily a day-and-a-half
phone without charging overnight,

00:11:17.522 --> 00:11:21.422
and it can sometimes be stretched into
a two-day-long battery life if you have

00:11:21.624 --> 00:11:23.431
have like a chill, light day...
Still,

00:11:23.513 --> 00:11:26.545
with all of my high-brightness
use and all my photo-taking...

00:11:26.627 --> 00:11:28.894
CarPlay for two hours every day,
everything...

00:11:28.976 --> 00:11:29.915
that is pretty sick.

00:11:29.997 --> 00:11:32.138
But the thing is,
the battery's not bigger.

00:11:32.780 --> 00:11:33.610
It's,

00:11:33.692 --> 00:11:35.490
maybe it's like 3% bigger
or something like that.

00:11:35.572 --> 00:11:36.402
But the point is,

00:11:36.484 --> 00:11:39.885
it is not some massively larger or
more dense battery that is making

00:11:39.967 --> 00:11:41.580
this better battery performance.

00:11:42.460 --> 00:11:43.484
It's the A20 Pro.

00:11:43.566 --> 00:11:45.990
Still, it is all the efficiency gains...

00:11:46.072 --> 00:11:48.559
from the 2-nanometer architecture.
It's...

00:11:48.641 --> 00:11:51.379
It's silicon chops
instead of silicon-carbon.

00:11:51.461 --> 00:11:53.270
Imagine if they did both.
But yeah,

00:11:53.352 --> 00:11:56.154
they haven't actually changed
much with the battery.

00:11:56.236 --> 00:11:58.982
What they did change is
they added faster charging.

00:11:59.064 --> 00:12:00.701
And it is actually significant.

00:12:00.783 --> 00:12:02.808
After finally running this thing dead,

00:12:02.890 --> 00:12:06.191
I plugged it in on a 67-watt charger
and this thing pulled 45

00:12:06.273 --> 00:12:07.633
watts for quite a while...

00:12:07.715 --> 00:12:11.959
So their seven hours of video playback
after five minutes of wired charging...

00:12:12.041 --> 00:12:12.871
seems legit.

00:12:12.953 --> 00:12:16.506
And the Pro Max, by the way,
actually does have about a 10% larger...

00:12:16.588 --> 00:12:18.869
battery capacity than the last generation.

00:12:18.951 --> 00:12:22.060
So it seems like it's right
around 5,500 milliamp-hours.

00:12:22.510 --> 00:12:23.340
Which,

00:12:23.586 --> 00:12:26.500
another side note,
it's kind of crazy that Apple doesn't just

00:12:27.222 --> 00:12:28.052
tell us,

00:12:28.415 --> 00:12:29.245
right?

00:12:29.327 --> 00:12:31.526
I mean, you're a,
it's a smartphone, you're a tech company.

00:12:31.608 --> 00:12:32.438
Just,

00:12:32.654 --> 00:12:33.484
just tell us!

00:12:33.566 --> 00:12:36.600
That we have to wait for someone to
disassemble the phone to actually

00:12:36.682 --> 00:12:39.020
look and see what the capacity is...
It's funny,

00:12:39.102 --> 00:12:42.569
in Europe they have this SIM
card tray version of the phone,

00:12:42.651 --> 00:12:46.415
but they are required,
required to submit like the energy labels.

00:12:46.497 --> 00:12:48.900
So we get the actual numbers.
So we know...

00:12:48.982 --> 00:12:51.266
it's 4,056 milliamp-hours for the Pro...

00:12:51.348 --> 00:12:53.159
and 5,391 for the Pro Max.
Great.

00:12:53.801 --> 00:12:55.731
The US gets the eSIM-only version,

00:12:56.533 --> 00:12:59.290
so we think it'll be
roughly a few percent more.

00:12:59.372 --> 00:13:00.202
But again,

00:13:00.764 --> 00:13:02.397
we just have to wait and see.

00:13:02.479 --> 00:13:03.740
It'll be around 5,500.

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:05.410
Shout out to the EU.

00:13:05.492 --> 00:13:08.119
There's some other little things
that are new on this phone,

00:13:08.201 --> 00:13:09.031
too.
The C2 modem,

00:13:09.113 --> 00:13:11.641
that should also contribute to
efficiencies and battery life,

00:13:12.203 --> 00:13:13.033
and new colors.

00:13:13.115 --> 00:13:15.868
You've probably already seen this
new burgundy all over the place...

00:13:15.950 --> 00:13:16.780
I'm not gonna lie.

00:13:17.323 --> 00:13:18.320
I just think it's ugly.

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:19.716
I think it's an ugly color.

00:13:19.798 --> 00:13:23.356
But there's also a new Glacier Blue color,
which is sort of a light sky blue.

00:13:23.438 --> 00:13:25.106
I think it's nice.
And there's also...

00:13:25.188 --> 00:13:26.997
a new matte black which I've been using.

00:13:27.079 --> 00:13:29.267
Shows a bit more fingerprints
than I was hoping,

00:13:29.349 --> 00:13:30.827
but I don't care.
This is the one.

00:13:30.909 --> 00:13:31.914
I'm using it.
I love it.

00:13:31.996 --> 00:13:34.137
This is the greatest
color they've ever made...

00:13:34.219 --> 00:13:36.879
And the Dynamic Island also
does get a little bit smaller.

00:13:36.961 --> 00:13:38.044
For the first time ever,

00:13:38.536 --> 00:13:41.172
they've done this by moving
the infrared Face ID sensor,

00:13:41.254 --> 00:13:42.677
which used to be in the middle,

00:13:43.479 --> 00:13:46.164
over to the top left corner,
and it's behind the display.

00:13:46.646 --> 00:13:48.457
And this actually makes a lot of sense.

00:13:48.539 --> 00:13:50.884
I'm surprised they didn't do it earlier,
honestly.

00:13:50.966 --> 00:13:54.039
This is a sensor that doesn't need
to be a super high resolution,

00:13:54.121 --> 00:13:55.155
unlike a selfie camera.

00:13:55.237 --> 00:13:58.844
So they can just cut out some of the
pixels to shine the infrared through...

00:13:58.926 --> 00:14:00.689
And it's just as effective down there.

00:14:00.771 --> 00:14:04.212
And the fact that you need a microscope
to see it at that slightly lower

00:14:04.294 --> 00:14:05.534
pixel density in the corner

00:14:06.216 --> 00:14:09.265
is a pretty good testament to a
successful implementation there.

00:14:09.347 --> 00:14:12.299
It literally only caught my eye
in direct sunlight maybe once,

00:14:12.381 --> 00:14:14.746
just noticing a little
faded circle in the corner.

00:14:14.828 --> 00:14:15.658
So yeah,

00:14:15.740 --> 00:14:17.570
now three Live Activities fit
up at the top instead of two.

00:14:18.965 --> 00:14:20.185
Game-changer for somebody.

00:14:20.267 --> 00:14:21.430
At the end of the day,

00:14:21.512 --> 00:14:24.315
my take on this phone is
it really isn't surprising

00:14:24.957 --> 00:14:26.345
at all.
Of course it isn't.

00:14:26.427 --> 00:14:27.477
It's the Pro iPhone.

00:14:27.559 --> 00:14:31.663
For years it's been the one that's
kind of treated as like a semi-finished

00:14:31.745 --> 00:14:35.000
product and it just gets these
slow evolutions over time...

00:14:35.082 --> 00:14:35.912
No crazy risks.

00:14:35.994 --> 00:14:39.812
The last Pro iPhone was one of the
bigger changes they've made in a while.

00:14:39.894 --> 00:14:41.926
It has obviously the new metal design...

00:14:42.008 --> 00:14:46.101
and the thicker new chassis with the
bigger batteries and the camera plateau...

00:14:46.183 --> 00:14:50.117
But even a lot of the little things,
like the new 3,000 nits max brightness,

00:14:50.199 --> 00:14:52.919
and the PWM dimming,
and the anti-reflective coating.

00:14:53.001 --> 00:14:54.671
So if that was a big tick...

00:14:54.753 --> 00:14:55.673
in the tick-tock

00:14:56.235 --> 00:14:57.216
cycle of updates,

00:14:58.098 --> 00:15:00.082
then this is a pretty good...
tock

00:15:00.564 --> 00:15:01.394
update.

00:15:01.476 --> 00:15:04.800
The 2-nanometer chip is doing a
lot of the heavy lifting here.

00:15:04.882 --> 00:15:08.430
And the variable aperture camera,
it's subtle if anything,

00:15:08.512 --> 00:15:10.683
but it has potential future value...

00:15:10.765 --> 00:15:11.889
as cameras evolve.

00:15:11.971 --> 00:15:14.423
So is the iPhone 18 Pro perfect?
No...

00:15:14.505 --> 00:15:16.204
Is it expensive?
Hell yeah.

00:15:16.286 --> 00:15:19.423
Is it exactly what we were expecting also?
Yeah.

00:15:19.505 --> 00:15:21.947
And there's some value to that, too.

00:15:22.029 --> 00:15:25.764
So get subscribed if you haven't already,
because there's a lot more coming up.

00:15:25.846 --> 00:15:27.165
It's Techtember, after all...

00:15:27.247 --> 00:15:28.083
And you know what??

00:15:28.165 --> 00:15:31.611
I think I've also kind of picked up
on channel sponsor dbrand's playbook,

00:15:31.693 --> 00:15:34.848
because it seems like every time
there's a new generation iPhone...

00:15:34.930 --> 00:15:37.129
they also release a new
category of phone case.

00:15:37.211 --> 00:15:38.041
You know,

00:15:38.123 --> 00:15:40.251
two years ago it was the Ghost
Case with the iPhone 16 Pro...

00:15:40.333 --> 00:15:41.163
And I gotta say,

00:15:41.245 --> 00:15:44.354
it's looking great on the 18 Pro now
that Apple's making black phones again.

00:15:44.436 --> 00:15:46.495
And if you've got a burgundy phone,
don't worry,

00:15:46.577 --> 00:15:48.636
they've got a color-matched
Ghost Case for that,

00:15:48.718 --> 00:15:49.548
too.

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:51.580
But then last year they launched
the Tank Case for the 17 Pro,

00:15:51.662 --> 00:15:54.301
and that's back and still looks
just as rugged on the 18 Pro,

00:15:54.383 --> 00:15:55.213
too.

00:15:55.295 --> 00:15:56.640
But that brings us to this
year and their latest launch.

00:15:57.400 --> 00:15:58.230
Minimal.

00:15:58.312 --> 00:15:59.804
And you probably guessed
just from the name,

00:15:59.886 --> 00:16:02.280
but Minimal is just a really clean...
minimalist case.

00:16:02.362 --> 00:16:04.054
Comes in four colors, and I gotta say,

00:16:04.136 --> 00:16:06.623
it's got this little
sandstone-ish texture to the back,

00:16:06.705 --> 00:16:07.535
too.

00:16:07.617 --> 00:16:09.420
It kind of reminds me of the
old-school OnePlus phones.

00:16:09.660 --> 00:16:12.099
And you can pick up a Prism
alongside your Minimal case

00:16:12.181 --> 00:16:13.406
to save 10 bucks in a bundle.

00:16:13.488 --> 00:16:14.398
Super easy to install,

00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:17.803
highly recommended if you're looking
for a screen protector for the iPhone.

00:16:17.885 --> 00:16:18.715
So yeah,

00:16:18.797 --> 00:16:19.783
tons of dbrand stuff
for these new iPhones.

00:16:19.865 --> 00:16:21.996
I'll leave a link down below
if you want to check it out.

00:16:22.078 --> 00:16:22.908
Or also,

00:16:22.990 --> 00:16:25.260
you can go to a Best Buy in the US and
check it out in person for yourself.

00:16:26.220 --> 00:16:28.240
Either way, thanks for watching.

00:16:28.962 --> 00:16:31.110
Catch you in the next one...
peace.

